# Environment contract for resync. Copy to `.env.local` and adjust.
#
# PROVIDER AND MODEL
#   AI_PROVIDER  openrouter | groq. Optional: when only one provider's key is
#                present, that provider is used; with none or both, OpenRouter is
#                the primary. Model ids stay vendor-shaped in MODEL_ID, but which
#                vendor they are sent to is this setting, not part of the name.
#   MODEL_ID     Optional. Defaults to the chosen provider's own default:
#                  openrouter -> openrouter/free
#                  groq       -> llama-3.3-70b-versatile
#   Keys         OPENROUTER_API_KEY / GROQ_API_KEY. Server-side only; never sent
#                to the browser. With both keys configured, the other provider is
#                used automatically when the first cannot route the request, or
#                when its free allowance is spent — that is the point of having two.
#
# AI_MODE
#   live  Calls the configured provider.
#   mock  Every AI call is served from a fixture recorded by the feature that
#         makes the call: no network, no key, fully deterministic.
#
# Which mode applies, in order:
#   1. an explicit AI_MODE here always wins;
#   2. otherwise any non-empty API key means live — a configured key is treated as
#      a request to use it, never as something to ignore quietly;
#   3. otherwise production means live, and fails loudly without a key;
#   4. otherwise mock, so a fresh clone runs with no setup.
#
# If a run is answering from fixtures, the app says so in a banner at the top of
# every page: mock mode replaces your own resume and posting with stored samples,
# so it must never look like a successful parse.
AI_MODE=

# Optional. Ordered models tried when the provider cannot route the primary one.
# A bare id belongs to the primary provider; `provider@model` targets the other
# one, e.g. groq@llama-3.3-70b-versatile. Blank keeps the built-in default list.
# `@` is the separator because model ids already contain `:` (openrouter's
# `:free` variants) and `/` (vendor prefixes). Listing only the configured model
# leaves nothing to fall back to; setting this replaces the default list exactly.
FALLBACK_MODEL_IDS=

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Free-tier allowances are per key and shared:
#   OpenRouter  20 requests/minute, 50 requests/day below $10 of credits (1000/day above)
#   Groq        per-model limits, listed in their console
